  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Y∼N(8,{3}^{2}),$ compute $P(Y\\ge 1.88).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0129\\,$ | $\\,0.0125\\,$ | $\\,0.0122\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.0166\\,$ | $\\,0.0162\\,$ | $\\,0.0158\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0207\\,$ | $\\,0.0202\\,$ |\n\n$P(Y\\ge 1.88)=$\n{{field-1}}",
